<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Iris runs under the hardened runtime, which notarization requires.

  This file is deliberately empty. Iris is a Rust binary plus a WKWebView: the
  web content runs in Apple's own out-of-process WebContent service, so the host
  app needs no JIT or unsigned-memory exception the way an Electron app does.
  It links only system frameworks, loads no third-party dylibs, and reads no
  DYLD_* variables, so library validation and the DYLD restrictions can stay on.

  `git` and `node` are launched as ordinary child processes, which the hardened
  runtime allows without an entitlement — they inherit nothing from Iris.

  Add an entitlement here only with a note saying which call needs it. Every one
  of these is a hole in the runtime protections that notarization is checking.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
